# One identity: Cato <41178744+catomean@users.noreply.github.com>
#
# Rewrites the DISPLAYED author of existing commits (git log, git shortlog,
# GitHub) without rewriting a single hash. Several names and addresses
# accumulated here before the git config was corrected.
#
# The canonical identity is always on the LEFT. A retired name on the left is
# the bug this file replaces: it renders every commit under the retired name,
# including new ones that were authored correctly.
#
# Three forms are used below:
#   `Cato <canonical>`                    - any name on the canonical address.
#   `Cato <canonical> <old-email>`        - matches by commit email alone.
#   `Cato <canonical> Name <that-email>`  - name + email, the narrowest form.

# Any name ever used on the canonical address resolves to Cato.
Cato <41178744+catomean@users.noreply.github.com>

# Retired noreply addresses (numbered and unnumbered forms of both accounts)
Cato <41178744+catomean@users.noreply.github.com> <41178744+maonakamoto@users.noreply.github.com>
Cato <41178744+catomean@users.noreply.github.com> <maonakamoto@users.noreply.github.com>
Cato <41178744+catomean@users.noreply.github.com> <41178744+g-but@users.noreply.github.com>

# The unnumbered form of the current noreply address
Cato <41178744+catomean@users.noreply.github.com> <catomean@users.noreply.github.com>

# The uninitialised default, used before a git config existed here
Cato <41178744+catomean@users.noreply.github.com> <your.email@example.com>

# The assistant's own commits stay the assistant's.
Claude (AI assistant) <noreply@anthropic.com> <noreply@anthropic.com>
